Z||000001||Cheever2||08-15-2001||12:19 AM||||My rock-bottom price for one w/ 83,000 miles is $3500 to Forum members, but it looks like I won't get that much here.<P>It's been real depressing to see the prices going <I>down</I>, not up.  That's good for <I>you</I>, the buyer, however.  <P>Is it in excellent condition?  Does it need anything (stupid question, it's a Fiero)?  How many previous owners?  Been on salty roads?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero11||08-15-2001||12:23 AM||||the fiero is in very good shape inside and out the only thing it needs is tires||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever2||08-15-2001||12:33 AM||||That's very low miles, and there's the sunroof.  If it's sparkling clean (show quality), and doesn't need any mechanicals, it's possible they might want as much as $5000 (US dollars) for it.  It all depends on what it's worth to <I>them</I>, and what it's worth to <I>you</I>.  Do some looking in the Mall section to see what people have been asking.  And compare what's on AutoTrader.com and eBay.<P>||||reg||1
